Tiny LLM (nanoapps/apps/tinyllm) is nano7kit's own code, MIT (see LICENSE
at the top of the repository).

tllm.c follows the forward pass, sampler and BPE tokenizer of llama2.c by
Andrej Karpathy, https://github.com/karpathy/llama2.c, MIT licence,
Copyright (c) 2023 Andrej. The text is in LICENSES/llama2.c-MIT.txt. The
code here is a rewrite for a soft-float Cortex-A5 (int8 weights, int8
activations, fixed-point attention), not a copy of run.c.

The model weights are not in this repository. They are the stories260K
checkpoint and tok512 tokenizer from karpathy/tinyllamas on Hugging Face,
https://huggingface.co/karpathy/tinyllamas, MIT licence, trained on the
TinyStories dataset. host/tinyllm.py downloads them at a pinned commit,
checks their SHA-256 sums and runs mkmodel.py on your computer to make
/Apps/Data/TinyLLM/model.bin.
